  "name": "Example: Calculating a Multiple of a Vector",
  "problem": "Let $[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ Find $\\dfrac{1}{2} \\mathbf{a}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Multiplying each component of $\\mathbf{a}$ by $\\dfrac{1}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}a & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-4) \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
